 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:10:33.761913Z",
 "text": "Under the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, a landlord cannot increase the rent for a residential rental unit without first giving the tenant at least **90 days'** written notice in the approved form. Any rent increase lacking the required 90-day notice is void under subsection 116(4) (and under section 4, landlords and tenants cannot contract out of the Act's requirements). Because this clause purports to allow a rent increase with only 30 days' written notice, it is void and unenforceable.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 116",
